RS.14 wrote:
> I was playing a barbarian a few days ago (no longer--killed by
> Demogorgon), but I realized that, with my boots of speed, I could
> simply wait for cockatrices to step next to me; hit them, step away,
> and repeat until they were dead. There doesn't seem to be any risk:
> they couldn't hit me at all. Why have I never heard about this? Does
> anyone else use this?
> BTW, I tried in wiz mode; there is some risk without you're speed
> boosted in some way, but it seems very small.

	There are a fair few critters that are significantly slower than
a normal-speed PC, and quite a lot that are slower than a fast or very
fast PC. This tactic works wonderfully against most of them. (Add a pole
arm, and you've got a safety buffer in case you get the timing wrong.)
It's useful in the Mines - both gnomes and dwarves are slow - and
*really* useful in shops - mimics are really slow, but hit hard enough
to one-shot low level characters, so never letting them have that shot
is a good strategy.

